## Update Orders [/v1/orders/batch-update]
<a name="update-orders"></a>

### Update Orders [PUT]
**⚠️ DEPRECATED** — as of 31.07.2026, use [PUT /v2/orders/batch-update](#update-orders-v2) instead.

Use to update order status, tracking information and actual delivery date.

If [Get orders](#get-orders) or [Get order](#get-order) contains *serialNumbers* then request body have to
contain all missing serials numbers. Please check [Serial numbers](#serial-numbers) section.

Pay attention to the response body. During the batch-update some validation errors can occur. Then the fields "hasErrors" and "errors" will contain relevant information, even though the response http status code is 200.
Possible errors:
```"Missing required field '{}'."```
```"Missing required field '{}' at parent '{}'."``` (in nested fields)
```"Status change {} is not repeatable."```
```"Change to status {} is not allowed from status {}."```
```"Order {} using Mall delivery cannot be updated after it has been shipped."```
```"Order {} does not have shipping labels created."``` (when trying to switch to SHIPPED for MALL orders managed by partner)
```"Order {} does not have a shipment created."``` (when trying to switch to SHIPPED for ALZA orders managed by partner)
```"Actual delivery date may only be filled when changing status from SHIPPED to DELIVERED ({})."```
```"Order delivery is managed by eshop. Actual delivery date field is not allowed."```
```"Field {} contains value {} that is not allowed. Allowed values are: {}"```
```"Status change {} is not allowed when order is in UPDATE_PENDING"```
```"Serial numbers are not filled for order id {}."``` (When all serial numbers are not filled for order id)

+ Request (application/json)
    + Headers
                
                Authorization: Bearer SIsImlhdCI6MTUxNjIzOTAyMn0
                
    + Attributes (UpdateOrderList)
    
+ Request Cancellation request example (application/json)
    + Headers
                
                Authorization: Bearer SIsImlhdCI6MTUxNjIzOTAyMn0
                
    
    + Body
    
                {
                  "orders": [
                    {
                      "id": "324GHdf87b",
                      "originalId": "987654321",
                      "status": "CANCELLED",
                      "cancellationReference": "Test cancellation reference",
                      "cancelReason": "OUT_OF_STOCK"
                    }
                  ]
                }

+ Response 200 (application/json)
    + Attributes (OrderList)

## Update Orders v2 [/v2/orders/batch-update]
<a name="update-orders-v2"></a>

### Update Orders v2 [PUT]

Use to update order status, tracking information and actual delivery date.

If [Get orders v2](#get-orders-v2) or [Get order v2](#get-order-v2) contains *serialNumbers* then request body have to
contain all missing serials numbers. Please check [Serial numbers](#serial-numbers) section.

Pay attention to the response body. During the batch-update some validation errors can occur. Then the fields "hasErrors" and "errors" will contain relevant information, even though the response http status code is 200.
Possible errors:
```"Missing required field '{}'."```
```"Missing required field '{}' at parent '{}'."``` (in nested fields)
```"Status change {} is not repeatable."```
```"Change to status {} is not allowed from status {}."```
```"Order {} using Mall delivery cannot be updated after it has been shipped."```
```"Order {} does not have shipping labels created."``` (when trying to switch to SHIPPED for MALL orders managed by partner)
```"Order {} does not have a shipment created."``` (when trying to switch to SHIPPED for ALZA orders managed by partner)
```"Actual delivery date may only be filled when changing status from SHIPPED to DELIVERED ({})."```
```"Order delivery is managed by eshop. Actual delivery date field is not allowed."```
```"Field {} contains value {} that is not allowed. Allowed values are: {}"```
```"Status change {} is not allowed when order is in UPDATE_PENDING"```
```"Serial numbers are not filled for order id {}."``` (When all serial numbers are not filled for order id)

+ Request (application/json)
    + Headers
                
                Authorization: Bearer SIsImlhdCI6MTUxNjIzOTAyMn0
                
    + Attributes (UpdateOrderList)
    
+ Request Cancellation request example (application/json)
    + Headers
                
                Authorization: Bearer SIsImlhdCI6MTUxNjIzOTAyMn0
                
    
    + Body
    
                {
                  "orders": [
                    {
                      "id": "324GHdf87b",
                      "originalId": "987654321",
                      "status": "CANCELLED",
                      "cancellationReference": "Test cancellation reference",
                      "cancelReason": "OUT_OF_STOCK"
                    }
                  ]
                }

+ Response 200 (application/json)
    + Attributes (OrderListV2)

## Print Labels [/v1/orders/{orderId}/labels{?returnOnlyUrl}]

+ Parameters
    + orderId: `1236548651` (number, required) - Id of the order as referenced in your system.
    + returnOnlyUrl: true (boolean, optional) - if specified and set to true no PDF file with shipping label will be returned, only location header will be present with url to generated shipping label. This is due to compatibility reasons.
    
### Print existing labels [GET]

+ Use to print existing shipping label without regenerating it.
+ In case of a missing shipping label for an order (e.g., label has not yet been generated), an error response will be returned.

Missing label error response:
```
{
  "httpStatus":404,
  "code":"NOT_FOUND",
  "codeDescription":"The specified resource or entity has not been found",
  "details":"Order with partnerId XXXXX does not have a generated label."
}
```


+ Request Request example
    + Headers
                
                Authorization: Bearer SIsImlhdCI6MTUxNjIzOTAyMn0
        
    
+ Response 200 (application/pdf)
    + Headers
    
            Content-Disposition: attachment;filename=shipping_labels.pdf"
            Location: url-to-generated-shipping-label

+ Response 204 (No Content)
    + Headers

            Location: url-to-generated-shipping-label

+ response 404 (application/json)

    + Body

                {
                    "httpStatus": 404,
                    "code": "NOT_FOUND",
                    "codeDescription": "The specified resource or entity has not been found",
                    "details": "Order with partnerId 4321425813 not found."
                }
### Generate Shipping Labels [POST]

+ Use to generate shipping labels for the orders, where the shipping is provided by the sales channel. Such orders are marked with "managedByPartner": false.
You can create new labels up till the order status is changed to `shipped`.
+ There are two different means of using this method. These are determined by the value in 'ShippingLabelsPrintMethod' on the order.
    1. *SIMPLE*: Only number of packages needs to be specified.
    2. *DETAILED*: You must specify details for each individual package. You do not need to specify the number of packages using this method, however it is still allowed. You can either use dimensions for your package or volume.
+ Items of the order can be split into several packages, even if they are the same item. If only one item fits into a single package, meaning that 2 same items will need to be shipped in 2 packages, you should reflect this in your request
to print the labels. This will result in different labels for the two packages, even if they contain the same item.
+ Furthermore, a single item can be split into several packages (the said item might be too big or is simply shipped in more parts) In this case, you should request for as many packages as you need, all of the packages will contain
valid information about this item, but only one of them will have count of 1, the others will list the item but will specify count 0.
+ It is possible to generate max. 3 labels for an order.



Sample validation error response:
```
{
  "httpStatus": 400,
  "code": "VALIDATION_ERROR",
  "codeDescription": "Validation of request failed",
  "details": "popis"
}
```
Additional possible details:
```"Order with partnerId {} not found."``` (status 404)
```"Cannot request labels for order original ID {}. Order is managed by partner."```
```"Cannot request labels for order original ID %s. Order's status is {}."```
```"Label print for order {} failed in MALL API. Details: {}"``` (describes error from MALL API)
```"Order {} shipment deletion failed in ALZA API. Details: {}"``` (when requesting new ALZA labels, the previous labels - and shipment - have to be deleted first)
```"Order {} shipment creation failed in ALZA API. Details: {}"```


+ Request Simple request example (application/json)
    + Headers
                
                Authorization: Bearer SIsImlhdCI6MTUxNjIzOTAyMn0
                
    + Attributes (RequestShippingLabels)
    
    + Body
    
                {
                    "numberOfPackages": 3
                }
    
        
    
+ Response 200 (application/pdf)
    + Headers
    
            Content-Disposition: attachment;filename=shipping_labels.pdf"
            Location: url-to-generated-shipping-label

+ Response 201
    + Headers
    
            Location: url-to-generated-shipping-label
            
+ Response 202
    + Headers
    
            Location: url-to-generated-shipping-label

+ Request Detailed request example (application/json)
    + Headers
                
                Authorization: Bearer SIsImlhdCI6MTUxNjIzOTAyMn0
                
    + Body
    
            {   "numberOfPackages": 2,
                "packages": [
                    {
                        "packageId": 1,
                        "weight": 4300,
                        "dimension1": 12,
                        "dimension2": 6,
                        "dimension3": 8,
                        "items": [
                            {
                                "id": "A25253FG",
                                "count": 1
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "packageId": 2,
                        "weight": 4300,
                        "volume": 576,
                        "items": [
                            {
                                "id": "A25253FG",
                                "count": 1
                            },
                            {
                                "id": "E25433FF",
                                "count": 3
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ]
            }

        
    
+ Response 200 (application/pdf)
    + Headers
    
            Content-Disposition: attachment;filename=shipping_labels.pdf"
            Location: url-to-generated-shipping-label

+ Response 201
    + Headers
    
            Location: url-to-generated-shipping-label

## Request Shipping Labels - batch [/v1/orders/labels]

### Generate Shipping Labels [POST]

Use for asynchronous request to generate shipping labels for multiple orders at once. Endpoint will return **requestId**, which will be used to get status of request processing. It will also return summary of how many orders were labels requested for as well as any validation errors. The request will be processed as long as at least one of the orders has passed thru initial MPI validation.
+ **orderSource** needs to be specified in request together with at least one of the order identifiers (**orderId** or **originalOrderId**).
+ Providing **numberOfPackages** or filling in detail for each package from the order is optional. If none of mentioned is sent, MPI will use product data to request correct amount of labels. If you specify **numberOfPackages** or fill in detail for each package, the calculation is not done byl MPI algorithm, but data you provided are used instead of product data.
+ Each order will be validated in MPI first, before being processed further. Any orders, that do not pass validation will be returned in the list **validationErrors** with detailing the reason for failing the validation.

Sample validation error response:
```
{
  "code": "WRONG_ORDER_STATUS",
  "message": "Order must be in status SHIPPING"
}
```
Possible validation errors

|code|message|
|-|-|
|`ORDER_NOT_FOUND`|`Order not found`|
|`WRONG_ORDER_TYPE`|`Order must have managedByPartner = false`|
|`WRONG_ORDER_STATUS`|`Order must be in status SHIPPING`|
|`WRONG_REQUEST_PARAMETERS`|`Order cannot be split into requested number of packages`|
|`WRONG_REQUEST_PARAMETERS`|`Labels were already requested in different request, which is being processed`|

+ Request Simple request example (application/json)
    + Headers

                Authorization: Bearer SIsImlhdCI6MTUxNjIzOTAyMn0

    + Attributes
        + orders (Order)
             + One of
                + properties
                    + numberOfPackages: 4 (number, required) - The number of packages, the order will be shipped in. Corresponds to number of labels, that will be printed.
                + properties
                    + packages
                        + properties
                             + packageId: 1 (number, required) - package identifier for this request. Needs to be unique within single request
                             + One of
                                + properties
                                    + weight: 4300 (number, required) - The weight of the package in grams.
                                    + dimension1: 12 (number, optional) - First dimension of the package in cm.
                                    + dimension2: 6 (number, optional) - Second dimension of the package in cm.
                                    + dimension3: 8 (number, optional) - Third dimension of the package in cm.
                                    + items
                                        + id: `A25253FG` (string) - Product id from your system.
                                        + count: 3 (number) - Count of this product id in the package.
                                + properties
                                    + weight: 4300 (number, required) - The weight of the package in grams.
                                    + volume: 576 (number, optional) - Volume of the package in cm3.
                                    + items
                                        + id: `A25253FG` (string) - Product id from your system.
                                        + count: 3 (number) - Count of this product id in the package.
                                + properties
                                    + size: `SM` (enum[string], required) - Simplified identification of package size.
                                        + members
                                             + `XS` - weight up to 2kg, dimensions up to 20x30x20 cm
                                             + `S` - weight  up to 5kg, dimensions up to 40x30x30 cm
                                             + `SM` - weight  up to 10kg, dimensions up to 60x40x30 cm
                                             + `M` - weight  up to 15kg, dimensions up to 70x40x40 cm
                                             + `ML` - weight  up to 20kg, dimensions up to 80x40x50 cm
                                             + `L`- weight  up to 31kg, dimensions up to 90x40x50 cm
                                             + `XL` - weight  up to 50kg, dimensions up to 120x80x90 cm
                                             + `XXL` - weight  up to 200kg, dimensions up to 120x160x120 cm
                                    + items
                                        + id: `A25253FG` (string) - Product id from your system.
                                        + count: 3 (number) - Count of this product id in the package.

    + Body

                {
                    "orders": [
                        {
                            "orderSource": "ALZA.CZ",
                            "orderId": "351236192",
                            "originalOrderId": "4504330851"
                        },
                        {
                            "orderSource": "MALL.CZ",
                            "orderId": "338730013",
                            "originalOrderId": "13270926102"
                        },
                        {
                            "orderSource": "MALL.CZ",
                            "orderId": "338730014",
                            "originalOrderId": "13270926103"
                        },
                        {
                            "orderSource": "MALL.HU",
                            "orderId": "338730016",
                            "originalOrderId": "13270926105"
                        }

                    ]
                }

+ Request Number of packages is specified example (application/json)

    + Body

                {
                    "orders": [
                        {   "numberOfPackages": 2,
                            "orderSource": "ALZA.CZ",
                            "orderId": "351236192",
                            "originalOrderId": "4504330851"
                        },
                        {   "numberOfPackages": 1,
                            "orderSource": "MALL.CZ",
                            "orderId": "338730013",
                            "originalOrderId": "13270926102"
                        },
                        {   "numberOfPackages": 5,
