## Shipping labels request status  [/v1/orders/labels/batch/{requestId}]

### Get shipping labels request status [GET]

Use to get the status of previously sent request to generate labels in batch
+ Endpoint will return status for whole request, together with lists of orders that have been processed, are being processed and those resulted in error.

+ parameters
    + requestId: `af177cc7-5498-41e1-8f3a-96439a13b40d` (string) - RequestId generated by MPI.

+ Response 200 (application/json)
    + Headers


    + Attributes
        + requestStatus (LabelRequestStatus)
        + completed (array[OrderLabelUrl])
        + processing (array[Order])
        + erroneous (ResponseLabelsOrders)

+ Response 404 (application/json)
    + Headers

    + Attributes
        +
        
## Print existing shipping labels into one file  [/v1/orders/labels/merge{?format}]

### Print existing labels [POST]

Use to download multiple previously generated labels as one PDF file
+ if an issue with labels for only of the requested orders occures, error message will be returned. First instance of an error will stop the merge process, meaning the error response will always contain a single error only.
+ Only if all requested orders have label ready, single PDF file with appended labels will be returned.

+ Parameters
    + format (enum[MergeType]) - format to print labels
        + Members
            + A4
            + CONTINUOUS

+ Request (application/json)
    + Headers

                Authorization: Bearer SIsImlhdCI6MTUxNjIzOTAyMn0

    + Attributes
        + orders (array[Order])

+ Response 200 (application/pdf)
    + Headers

            Content-Disposition: attachment;filename=shipping_labels.pdf"

+ Response 404 (application/json)
    + Headers
    
    
    + Body
    
                {
                    "httpStatus": 404,
                    "code": "NOT_FOUND",
                    "codeDescription": "Existing label not found",
                    "details": "Failed to retreive existing label for order with original id {orderOriginalId} from source {orderSource}."
                }


